cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Praxis in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "Praxis — Browser and desktop polyglot IDE for Python and 29+ languages"
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  Praxis is a localhost-first browser and desktop polyglot IDE built with Next.js
  and Bun that turns a folder of scripts into an interactive workbench for Python
  and 29+ additional languages. Users can browse auto-discovered project trees,
  edit with syntax highlighting and Pyright LSP diagnostics, and execute code in
  place with streaming output, captured matplotlib figures, DataFrame previews,
  variable inspection, code coverage, profiling panels, and standalone desktop
  distributions for Windows, Linux, and macOS.
